Rem ===================================================================
Rem mungo-caverns-look.shoddy -- describing where you are standing.
Rem 
Rem Long description or short, what is lying here, and
Rem the darkness rule that decides whether you see any of it.
Rem ===================================================================

Rem ---- describing a room ----------------------------------------------------
Rem The long description shows on the first visit and
Rem every fifth after; the short one fills the gaps, unless the room has
Rem no short form.

Rem A room counts as forced when it has a travel row whose
Rem motion is the magic HERE. A forced room moves you straight on again,
Rem and it is shown even in the dark -- which is how ">>Foof!<<" gets
Rem seen at all.
Def HereMotion() As Number
    1

Def IsForced(g As Game) As Boolean
    Let k = Nth(Tkey(), Location(g) + 1)
    If k = 0 Then
        False
    Else
        Motion(RowAt(k)) = HereMotion()

Def RoomText(g As Game) As String
    If IsDarkHere(g) And Not IsForced(g) Then
        Nth(Messages(), MsgPitchDark() + 1)
    Else
        Let r = RoomAt(g)
        Let seen = Nth(LocationSeen(g), Location(g) + 1)
        If (seen Mod AbbrevInterval(g)) = 0 Or Len(Short(r)) = 0 Then
            Long(r)
        Else
            Short(r)

Rem Each object shows the description for its current
Rem state; an object with no descriptions is invisible scenery.
Rem The steps are one object standing in two rooms, and
Rem which way they lead depends on which end you are at -- they are
Rem special-cased right here rather than given two entries.
Def StateShown(g As Game, i As Number) As Number
    If i <> ObjNamed("STEPS") Then
        PropOf(g, i)
    Else
        Let ps = Places(ObjAt(i))
        If Length(ps) > 1 And Location(g) = Nth(ps, 2) Then
            1
        Else
            0

Def DescOf(g As Game, i As Number) As String
    Let o = ObjAt(i)
    Let p = StateShown(g, i)
    If IsEmpty(Descs(o)) Then
        ""
    Else
        If p >= 0 And p < Length(Descs(o)) Then
            Nth(Descs(o), p + 1)
        Else
            First(Descs(o))

Rem Once the nugget is in your hands the steps stop being
Rem worth mentioning, because you cannot climb them carrying it.
Def Skipped(g As Game, i As Number) As Boolean
    ((i = ObjNamed("STEPS") And Toting(g, ObjNamed("NUGGET")))
     Or (IsHidden(g, i) And Closed(g)))

Rem Describing a treasure for the first time is what
Rem marks it found and takes it off the tally -- the tally is what tells
Rem the cave when to start closing.
Rem Two treasures do not simply become "found": the rug
Rem is first seen with the dragon lying on it, and the chain with the bear
Rem chained to it, so they jump straight to that state.
Def FoundState(i As Number) As Number
    If i = ObjNamed("RUG") Or i = ObjNamed("CHAIN") Then
        1
    Else
        0

Def MarkFound(g As Game, i As Number) As Game
    If IsHidden(g, i) Then
        With(g, Props = SetNth(Props(g), i + 1, FoundState(i)),
                Tally = Tally(g) - 1,
                SeenBigWords = SeenBigWords(g) Or i = ObjNamed("EGGS"))
    Else
        g

Def ListObjects(g As Game, xs As List, i As Number, n As Number) As Game
    If i > n Then
        g
    Else
        If Skipped(g, Nth(xs, i)) Then
            ListObjects(g, xs, i + 1, n)
        Else
            Let g1 = MarkFound(g, Nth(xs, i))
            ListObjects(Voiced(g1, Grounded(g1, DescOf(g1, Nth(xs, i)))), xs, i + 1, n)

Rem Things described as "on the floor" have their floor
Rem quietly reworded to ground when you are out of doors -- only before
Rem a space, a full stop, or the end of the text, exactly as the
Rem original does.
Def Grounded(g As Game, msg As String) As String
    If Outside(g) And Location(g) <> LocNamed("LOC_BUILDING") Then
        GroundedAt(msg, 1, Len(msg), "")
    Else
        msg

Def GroundedAt(msg As String, i As Number, n As Number, acc As String) As String
    If i > n Then
        acc
    Else
        If (Mid(msg, i, 5) = "floor"
            And (i + 5 > n Or Mid(msg, i + 5, 1) = " "
                 Or Mid(msg, i + 5, 1) = ".")) Then
            GroundedAt(msg, i + 5, n, acc & "ground")
        Else
            GroundedAt(msg, i + 1, n, acc & Mid(msg, i, 1))

Rem In the dark you see nothing lying about, which is the whole point of
Rem the lamp. One line of atmosphere costs a random draw -- and only at
Rem Y2, because everywhere else the guard short-circuits before the roll.
Rem Drawing unconditionally desynchronises every seeded game.
Rem The two halves stay apart: the description always runs, but a forced
Rem room leaves before the listing. So the bear and the Y2 voice --
Rem and the random draw the voice costs -- belong to the description, not to
Rem the listing.
Def DescribeOnly(g As Game) As Game
    Let g0 = BearNote(g)
    Whisper(Voiced(g0, RoomText(g0)))

Def Describe(g As Game) As Game
    Let g1 = DescribeOnly(g)
    If IsDarkHere(g1) Then
        g1
    Else
        Let here = HereList(g1)
        ListObjects(g1, here, 1, Length(here))

Rem The bear announces himself ahead of the room, so the
Rem reminder that you are dragging him around lands before the description.
Def BearNote(g As Game) As Game
    If Toting(g, ObjNamed("BEAR")) Then
        VoicedId(g, MsgTameBear())
    Else
        g

Def Whisper(g As Game) As Game
    If Location(g) <> LocNamed("LOC_Y2") Then
        g
    Else
        Let hit = Pct(LcgState(g), 25)
        Let g1 = Stepped(g)
        If hit And Not ClosingTime(g1) Then
            VoicedId(g1, MsgSaysPlugh())
        Else
            g1

Def Visited(g As Game) As Game
    With(g, LocationSeen = SetNth(LocationSeen(g), Location(g) + 1, Nth(LocationSeen(g), Location(g) + 1) + 1))

